INT. TAXIDERMY SHOP - DAY

Glass eyes everywhere. A badger in a tutu. A moose wearing sunglasses.

BARNABY "BARNEY" QUIGLEY, 40s, apron, tweezers, is mid-surgery on a pheasant.

The bell jingles. In steps NADIA FONTAINE-OKAFOR, 30s, in a black dress and veil, holding a shoebox.

NADIA
Barney.

BARNEY
Nadia. Hey. Sorry. Don't touch the badger.

NADIA
I need Mr. Biscuit preserved.

BARNEY
Mr. Biscuit.

NADIA
My hamster.

BARNEY
Oh. Oh no.

NADIA
Don't "oh no" me. I paid eleven dollars to a priest.

BARNEY
Hamsters are tiny. The skin's like tissue. It's basically origami.

NADIA
Then fold him.

She puts the shoebox on the counter. Opens it. They both lean in.

BARNEY
He looks peaceful.

NADIA
He looks stuffed already.

BARNEY
That's rigor, Nadia.

NADIA
Don't say rigor in front of him.

BARNEY
Okay. Okay. Pose?

NADIA
Running on the wheel.

BARNEY
I don't have a wheel.

NADIA
You have a moose in sunglasses, Barney. Find a wheel.

BARNEY
That moose is a commissioned work.

NADIA
By whom?

BARNEY
A very rich man named Gus.

NADIA
Is Gus alive?

BARNEY
Barely. Moose, though. Moose is forever.

Nadia picks up the tweezers. Aims them at Barney like a tiny sword.

NADIA
Wheel. Hamster. Today.

BARNEY
Nadia, it's a three-week turnaround.

NADIA
Barney, he's thawing.

BARNEY
(grabbing the box)
Right. Wheel. Found one.

He sprints to the back. Crash. Squeak. A rubber duck rolls out.

NADIA
(calling)
That's a duck!

BARNEY (O.S.)
It's a start!
